# Puppet Crafting makes a Mox a creature, so summoning sickness applies (CR 302.6): Mox Ruby has been Bot1's since turn 1 and is
# enchanted at once, so on turn 3 it attacks as a 5/5 and deals 5 (20 -> 15). Mox Jet, which Bot1 draws and casts on turn 3 and
# enchants then, has not been under its control since the turn began: the attack with it is refused (beside Ruby's, the positive
# control) and, being a creature with a {T} ability, it can't tap for mana either; the Mox Emerald it doesn't touch still can.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald x2
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Puppet Crafting
Puppet Crafting
Mox Jet
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Puppet Crafting.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Puppet Crafting.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Power = 5
! Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Attack(Mox Jet > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Mox Ruby > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 15
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.SummoningSick = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.SummoningSick = false
